From 91bbb6f4e021e380223a3d73008d60064acac689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:02:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nethernet): accept BDS capability responses without
 metadata

The pinned BDS 1.26.51.1 endpoint returns an empty 200 response to its
capability probe. A native 26.51 client proceeds to the SDP exchange and
spawns successfully, while the newer transport rejects the missing JSON.

Provide the complete HTTP signaling flow in core for direct and proxy
clients. Use the capability status independently of optional metadata,
retain SDP and transport identity validation, cancel pending requests on
close, and reject certificate validation failures instead of downgrading.

Loopback tests cover native-style plaintext TLS rejection, empty capability
responses, unsupported endpoints, SDP delivery and invalid answers.

Share the existing self-signed game identity factory with transports so
HTTP clients can sign the offer before LOGIN_START and preserve the same
key through login. Exact BDS 1.26.51.1 protocol2193 rejects the unsigned
offer with numeric37 and opens ICE/DTLS with the self-signed assertion.
Token tests verify public-key binding and fresh reconnect keys.
